course: dictionary
lesson: 11452
title: Adjudicate: deciding fairly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To adjudicate means to make an official decision about a disagreement, or to judge who wins a contest. Someone who adjudicates has the power to decide, and they try to be fair.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «The referee had to adjudicate the match after the two teams argued about the goal.» The referee settles the argument, so adjudicate must mean to decide officially. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "The referee had to decide the match" still makes sense.
explain: Adjudicate is a formal word, so you will meet it most in serious writing, such as law reports and competition rules. Look for the phrases that often go with it: adjudicate a dispute, adjudicate a competition, adjudicate on a question, and adjudicate between two people.
fact: Adjudicate means to make an official decision about a disagreement or a contest.
fact: In law, a judge adjudicates a case by deciding it.
fact: At school or in sport, someone can adjudicate a competition by deciding who wins.
fact: Useful phrases: adjudicate a dispute, adjudicate a competition, adjudicate on, adjudicate between.
exercise: «The judges will adjudicate the singing contest on Friday.» What does adjudicate mean here? | *Decide who wins | Sing the loudest song | Cancel the contest | Carry the prizes home
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means to judge and decide: «Mrs Patel was asked to adjudicate the debate.» | asked | Patel | debate | *adjudicate
exercise: Ella says, "Adjudicate is just another word for argue." Why is she wrong? | Argue and adjudicate mean exactly the same thing | Adjudicate means to be very loud | *Adjudicate means to make an official decision, not to argue | Adjudicate is a name for a sport
test: «The court will adjudicate the dispute about the boundary fence.» What does the court have to do? | Build a new fence for them | Shout at both neighbours | *Make an official decision about the disagreement | Ask them to play a game
test: «Our head teacher will adjudicate between the two finalists in the spelling bee.» Which phrase best describes what she does? | She writes the spelling words on the board | She waves to the crowd | She eats the spare sweets | *She decides which finalist is better, fairly
exam: «The panel of judges must adjudicate the science fair.» What does adjudicate mean? | Set up the stalls for the fair | *Decide the winners of the science fair officially | Close the fair early because of rain | Visit the fair with friends
